{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the parameter prior statements so `lambda` is sampled with its built-in Cauchy prior before it is used in the scale of the `theta` prior. This preserves the same log density because Stan sampling statements contribute additively. The observation model `y ~ normal(theta[context_idx], sigma)` is unchanged; `K`, `N`, `context_idx`, `tau`, and `sigma` are context inputs and are not protected.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> K;                       // Number of groups
  int<lower=0> N;                       // Number of observations
  vector[N] y;                          // Observations
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> context_idx; // Context assignments
  real<lower=0> tau;                    // Base Population Scale
  real<lower=0> sigma;                  // Measurement variability
}

parameters {
  vector[K] theta;
  vector<lower=0>[K] lambda;
}

model {
  // Horseshoe prior model
  lambda ~ cauchy(0, 1);
  theta ~ normal(0, lambda * tau);

  // Observational model
  y ~ normal(theta[context_idx], sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":3,"N":1,"context_idx":[2],"sigma":4.45302261384107,"tau":1.0156631930056583,"y":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
